swift-sheet-music
=================

This Swift package provides libraries for working with engraved music
notation: parsing MuseScore (.mscx) files, modelling them as Swift value
types, and exporting them to MIDI. It is an unofficial implementation,
not affiliated with or endorsed by MuseScore Limited / Muse Group, nor
with Apple's `MusicKit` framework.

Source code license
-------------------

All Swift source code under `Sources/` (every `SheetMusic*` library
product) is licensed under the MIT License (see LICENSE in the project
root).

The implementation is independently authored. Algorithms (e.g. arpeggio
note timing, pause-aware tempo map handling, MeasureRepeat group
resolution, Volta-aware repeat playback) were studied from the MuseScore
C++ implementation (https://github.com/musescore/MuseScore, GPL-3.0) but
no source code is copied; the Swift implementation was rewritten from
scratch using the referenced behavior as a specification. Inline doc
comments occasionally cross-reference the originating MuseScore class or
function for traceability.

MuseScore is a trademark of Muse Group. Use of the name in this project's
documentation and code identifiers is nominative (to indicate file format
and behavioral compatibility) and does not imply affiliation.

Test fixtures
-------------

The mscx and reference MIDI files under `Tests/SheetMusicTests/Resources/`
are copies of test fixtures from the upstream MuseScore repository
(`src/importexport/midi/tests/midiexport_data/` in
<https://github.com/musescore/MuseScore>), used here to verify
byte/semantic equivalence with MuseScore's own MIDI exporter output.
These files are licensed under GPL-3.0; see
`Tests/SheetMusicTests/Resources/LICENSE`.

Because these fixtures are confined to the test target and are not
distributed as part of the published library products, they do not affect
the licence of code that depends on this package.

Third-party Swift dependencies
------------------------------

Resolved via Swift Package Manager (all Apache-2.0 licensed):

- swift-java — Apache 2.0 (https://github.com/swiftlang/swift-java)
- swift-subprocess — Apache 2.0 (https://github.com/swiftlang/swift-subprocess)
- swift-wirelet — Apache 2.0 (https://github.com/jiyimeta/swift-wirelet)

ZIP handling is implemented in-house (`Sources/SheetMusicZip`) over
Apple's `Compression` framework on Apple platforms and the system
`zlib` on Linux / Android; no third-party ZIP library is vendored.

Android audio module dependencies
---------------------------------

The Android playback module (Kotlin, `Android/SheetMusicAudioAndroid/`)
depends, at build time via Gradle, on:

- FluidSynth — LGPL-2.1 (https://github.com/VolcanoMobile/fluidsynth-android),
  dynamically linked as `libfluidsynth.so`; not vendored in this
  repository. Applications redistributing the module must honour
  LGPL-2.1 §4 (allow replacing the shared library, include the LGPL
  notice). See `Android/SheetMusicAudioAndroid/README.md`.
- Oboe — Apache 2.0 (https://github.com/google/oboe)

SoundFonts
----------

This package ships no audio samples; consumers supply a General MIDI
SoundFont through the `SoundfontResolver` protocol. The SoundFonts the
example apps reference are third-party and carry their own licenses:

- MuseScore_General by S. Christian Collins — the split per-program set
  is hosted at https://github.com/jiyimeta/musescore-general-sf2-split
- GeneralUser GS by S. Christian Collins —
  https://schristiancollins.com/generaluser.php

Any redistribution of these SoundFont binaries (for example via GitHub
Releases) must include their respective license text and attribution.

